WEBVTT

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.840
The following program is brought to you in living color on NBC.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.090
Maximum power, port shield.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:05.510
Aye, aye.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.140
Stabilize!

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.470
Stop brawling you great lumbering Karolva!

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:51.620
It's a girl!

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.460
Locking on target!

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.220
Turn fire!

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:54.800
Fire!

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.280
Scotty! Spock, report!

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.900
Our last two shots inflicted serious damage to their primary hull.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.070
They have changed course and are retreating beyond phaser range.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.980
Don't ever call this sh-

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.600
a big lumbering moose again.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.170
Moose? Cow.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.100
You've made a big mistake.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.640
There will be consequences, I assume.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.440
Space. Final Frontier.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.120
These are the new voyages of the starship Enterprise.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.680
Its five-year mission to explore strange new worlds.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.100
To seek out new life and new civilizations.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.310
To boldly go where no man has gone before.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.960
USS Enterprise, Captain's Personal Law.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:09.500
My nephew, Peter, has been assigned to the Enterprise as an incident with the Klingons.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.960
What dangers am I exposing you to?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.440
I haven't seen Peter in too many years.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.050
I don't even know him.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:25.100
Let me make him understand this isn't a game out here.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:41.940
Freeman get him out of here we've got real wounded I'm fine any day now Freeman

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:53.560
okay now you're done tell me a deep spanner you may have internal bleeding

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:59.910
yeah he's Peter Kirk but you treat him like everyone else

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.540
She got that?

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:02.820
Yes, sir.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.840
Fontana, go heal something.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.770
Freeman, you moved too long in the same place.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.270
Go help her.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.110
I've got this.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.320
It's a distress signal, sir.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:29.710
The Copernicus.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:30.960
A research vessel.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.460
We're in no shape to help.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:35.290
Who else is in this quadrant?

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:37.510
There are no other Starfleet vessels this far out.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:40.130
We are 10 hours away at warp factor 2.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:41.170
The Klingon ship?

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:42.850
He's no longer an immediate threat.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:43.970
Neither are we.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.010
Informed command will respond as best we can.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.390
Mr. Chekov, lay in a course.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.210
Scott, what speed can you give me?

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:55.410
Scott, I need warp factor 4.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.510
Warp factor 2.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.770
And not a wee bit more.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.020
Take knowledge. Mr. Chekov, I had Warp Factor 2.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:24.060
Captain's log supplemental. We are still several hours from the Copernicus, and her distress signal continues to repeat.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.890
I have asked Mr. Spock to assemble a mission team.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:38.490
Nope, not him. Take Freeman instead. He's a medical technician.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:44.300
Captain, is it possible you're being overprotective?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.200
He's not going.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.980
That's swaggering, tin-plated...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Stupid son of a bitch if he weren't my uncle at you seem upset. He took me off the mission team

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:14.290
You are taking this personally. Yes. I am he made it personal. He's afraid I'll fall off my bike again

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:20.170
You expect too much from him. He is only human. He's not human

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:28.680
He's James T. Kirk, and you want to be just like him. You are his nephew. I'm on duty now

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.680
You are in my way.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:32.780
Right.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.080
Have fun.

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:45.760
Fun.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:01.810
Guess who?

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.010
Mmm, Mr. Suli.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:06.620
You wish.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:19.910
I heard.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.720
I'm sorry, I don't know how much you wanted to go.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.420
There'll be other opportunities.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:39.270
Watch the burn.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:40.190
Ah, it still hurts.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:40.870
Yeah.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:41.790
Yeah, let me see.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:42.310
Careful.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.040
That could be worse.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:17.250
You make everything all right.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:19.170
Not this time.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:21.460
What?

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.290
They put me on the mission team.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:26.040
No.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:27.350
Yes.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:39.630
he knows about us let's see how he has to maybe he thinks i'm here because i wanted to serve under

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:49.900
him as such i'm here because of you

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.240
I got it.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:11.160
Will you marry me?

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:14.870
How many times are you going to ask me?

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:16.800
He said yes.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:17.220
No.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:21.260
Here, on the Enterprise.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:23.880
I'll ask him to do it.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:27.540
Say yes.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:32.920
Of course.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:36.280
You know him better than I do.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.020
What do you think you'll say?

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.550
I don't know him at all.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.530
We'll do it right after you finish rescuing everyone on the Copernicus.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.460
I wish I was going.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:49.840
I want you to go.

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.160
You've got to be brave for both of us now.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:58.900
Have I told you today?

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.950
how much I love you, Peter Kirk.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:10.960
I love you too, Alex Freeman Kirk.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:47.850
Red giant, blue dwarf, pear.

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:49.910
It's beautiful, Mr. Spock.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.940
The paired stars are far more interesting as a scientific phenomenon.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.330
The red giant is named Lear, after King Lear.

00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:58.910
The blue dwarf is Iago.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:01.840
Somebody didn't know their Shakespeare very well.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.040
A Russian wouldn't make that mistake.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.580
It is a metaphor, Mr. Chekhov.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:07.780
The red giant is a very old star.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:10.910
The blue-white dwarf is pulling the fire out of it.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:13.340
It will take thousands of centuries, of course.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:15.520
Still a spectacular view.

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:17.950
Mr. Chekhov, locate the Copernicus.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:20.900
There they are.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:29.830
Can't be right.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:34.770
Captain, the orbit will take them right into the streamer. They'll burn it up.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:38.180
How long?

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:39.600
18 hours.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:43.320
What kind of an idiot puts his ship in a self-destruction orbit?

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:46.510
Perhaps we should ask what kind of circumstance requires it.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:48.600
Life science, Mr. Spock.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.990
Indeterminate. There is too much interference to get a clear reading.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:12:59.280
Lieutenant O'Hora.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.810
Still no response, Captain. Nothing.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.380
Keep trying. Mr. Chekov, take us in.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.850
Match your orbit and put us within transporter range.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.560
What the hell is happening on that ship?

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.860
Captain's log started at 6429.2.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:47.810
We have matched orbit with the Copernicus, still unable to detect life signs.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.430
Scott has confirmed that we don't have the power to tow her out of danger.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.790
Before this day ends, the Copernicus will be a memory.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.750
The rescue party will search for survivors.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.760
and retrieve the log as quickly as possible.

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:05.460
Don't go try to beat a hero.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.850
We've already got enough heroes on this ship.

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:09.770
Yes, sir.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.630
Stretch too thin, Spock.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:19.170
Between our own casualties and the damage to the Enterprise,

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.030
if the Klingons should attack again.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.050
It is a risk we will have to take, Captain.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:25.230
The Copernicus will burn up in 12 hours.

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:25.990
Captain Kirk.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:27.410
Peter.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.060
Ensign Kirk, sir.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:31.900
Ensign Kirk?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:33.680
Permission to speak?

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:36.600
You took me off the mission team.

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:37.920
May I ask what?

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.060
It was the appropriate decision.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.990
What was appropriate about it, sir?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:44.400
Peter, this is-

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.320
Ensign Kirk.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:46.990
Ensign Kirk?

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.540
Sir, you could tell me it was an appropriate decision.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:52.800
And I'll believe you.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.090
But what about the rest of this crew?

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:57.260
I'm as well trained as anyone.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.490
And if I'm not put on a mission team-

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.920
Will it look to them as if you're trying to protect me?

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:06.000
And if the crew starts to believe that, I won't be able to function here.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:11.640
I'll have to ask for a transfer. And so will my husband.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:14.420
Husband?

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.300
Yes, if you'll marry us.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:23.020
Lieutenant Alex Freeman, medical technician.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.490
After this mission, sir.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:31.530
I see.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:35.900
We'll talk about it.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:37.520
After the mission.

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:41.310
I mean, setting a date for your wedding.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:44.130
Thank you, sir.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:50.660
And I guess, congratulations are an order, aren't they, Ensign?

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:51.820
Yes, sir.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:53.680
Thank you, sir.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:59.980
Ensign, I'm here to join the mission team.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.190
Yes, sir. Very much, sir.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:05.420
Go get your gear.

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:14.660
Spock, am I the only one who didn't know?

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:19.420
I believe Mr. Scott might have been too busy to notice.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:46.670
30 seconds to optimal range let's find a safe place to put them down picking up hard interference

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:54.930
from the cargo bay interesting it is a series of concentric repulsor fields repulsor fields

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:59.770
at that strength they'd have to be using the ships to remain in power they must be trying to contain

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.380
That would be a logical assumption.

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:19.490
Yes. You owe me 20.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.590
You'll have to work fast, Fock. That beacon is a signal.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.010
If the Klingons should pick it up.

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.620
I'm certain they already have.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.960
We must move quickly, Lieutenant Randall.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.820
Rand, come with me.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.240
Rand, Hodel, your first priorities.

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:39.820
Retrieve the log of the Copernicus.

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:41.140
Shut down the distress signal.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.860
Freeman, Dassault, look for survivors.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.420
Ensign, stay with me.

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:49.050
Mr. Spock, be careful.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:50.540
Of course, Captain.

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:52.600
Energize.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.740
My nephew on a security team.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.210
Relax, Jim.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:10.710
We don't put bullseyes in the red shirts anymore.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:04.500
Do that again.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:15.900
Wave of course.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.240
A phenomenon that demonstrates the characteristics

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.560
of both wave and particle.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:23.380
You mean it can make up its mind

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:24.580
what it wants to be when it grows up?

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:28.190
Lieutenant, particles do not have minds.

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:34.330
Hey, that tickles.

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:35.210
Mr. Freeman.

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:50.920
Sorry, sir.

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:56.240
Properties of wavicles are in constant flux.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:58.800
That's why your tricorder readings are confused.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.260
We would need a magnetonic deconstructor

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.460
to isolate the transactions.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:05.820
Wow.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:29.400
Rich.

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:30.990
It's been welded shut.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:35.170
Captain.

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:36.550
Are you picking this up?

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.310
We'll see it tomorrow.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:47.960
Lieutenant.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:50.990
Ask Starfleet Command for a Code 9 review.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:52.660
Acknowledged.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.280
He sent the distress signal.

00:22:16.340 --> 00:22:17.020
Mr. Freeman.

00:22:18.220 --> 00:22:20.020
Sir, there's no blood in this man's body.

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:21.270
Blood at all.

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:23.710
Mr. Spock.

00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:36.160
That's a phaser blast, Mr. Spock.

00:22:37.110 --> 00:22:37.470
Clearly.

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.220
Check the consoles.

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:42.600
Mr. Odell, Lieutenant Rand, the log, the beacon.

00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:55.950
Oh, this console's been destroyed.

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:06.860
You're too, Mr. Spock.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:18.670
Spock, it's the whole damn bridge.

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:36.760
Captain, I'm getting some kind of movement on the Copernicus. Life signs, I think.

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:39.330
Location.

00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:46.510
Very strange. I can't get the focus. But it looks like it's headed toward the bridge.

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:47.750
Spock, did you copy that?

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:49.780
Acknowledged.

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:59.980
I'm getting something. I'm reading it, too. It's stronger. Coming from...

00:24:07.450 --> 00:24:12.660
You can bake, you're all dead, everyone's dead.

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:16.180
You'll see, you're next.

00:24:16.590 --> 00:24:18.760
All of you, you're next!

00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:20.060
What's your name, Kruman?

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:25.560
Aaron's, what are you doing?

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:26.680
It'll help with the pain.

00:24:27.760 --> 00:24:28.910
Oh, no!

00:24:30.350 --> 00:24:31.570
WHAT HAVE YOU DONE?!

00:24:32.460 --> 00:24:33.400
IT'S HAPPENING!

00:24:34.740 --> 00:24:35.280
KILL ME!

00:24:35.580 --> 00:24:35.980
ENTERPRISE

00:24:35.980 --> 00:24:37.000
PLEASE KILL ME!

00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:39.020
THE MYSTERIOUS LIFE FORMS ARE HERE, AN ENTERED ROOM

00:24:39.020 --> 00:24:40.260
NO, THAT'S NOT WHAT I'M READING!

00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:42.740
WHATEVER IT IS, IT'S STILL MOVING TOWARDS YOU!

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:43.560
DAMN YOU!

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:44.900
SAFE!

00:25:26.810 --> 00:25:27.470
Surprising knowledge.

00:25:30.520 --> 00:25:31.820
We did.

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:37.030
Captain, we have to assume this entire ship is contaminated.

00:25:39.220 --> 00:25:39.600
Gentlemen.

00:25:40.790 --> 00:25:41.030
Options.

00:25:42.580 --> 00:25:46.000
Scotty, what about the transporters biofilter?

00:25:47.050 --> 00:25:48.810
The beam won't allow the particle to form.

00:25:49.040 --> 00:25:50.780
That'll certainly replicate the wave component.

00:25:51.240 --> 00:25:51.900
And that'll be enough.

00:25:52.390 --> 00:25:53.170
They'll slip right through.

00:25:53.390 --> 00:25:56.400
Can we beam them to an isolation bay inside a repulsor field?

00:25:57.080 --> 00:25:58.380
If it was strong enough, maybe.

00:25:59.160 --> 00:25:59.960
But one repulsor field...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.360
field won't be enough. You need at least six or seven concentric fields. And even then,

00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:12.190
cannot guarantee field integrity. Not in our present condition. Captain, the mission team will

00:26:12.190 --> 00:26:20.110
not beam back. We cannot risk infecting the Enterprise. Do you agree? I do, Spock. The

00:26:20.110 --> 00:26:28.440
safety of the Enterprise must come first. Spock, I need that ship's log. Find it. Knowledge. Spock out.

00:26:32.080 --> 00:26:34.120
Jim, we need to talk.

00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:35.040
Turbolift.

00:26:35.690 --> 00:26:44.710
Oh, Jim.

00:26:45.080 --> 00:26:47.080
Bones, we're thinking the same thing.

00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:48.400
Plasmasites.

00:26:50.220 --> 00:26:51.260
Damn bloodworms.

00:26:51.420 --> 00:26:52.400
Regulin bloodworms.

00:26:52.520 --> 00:26:55.540
The entire Regulin system's been under quarantine for over 100 years.

00:26:55.850 --> 00:26:57.270
I mean, how in the hell could this happen?

00:26:57.540 --> 00:26:59.180
The Copernicus must have violated that quarantine.

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:07.930
blood worms broke out bones you've got to find an answer i know i know you're a doctor not a miracle

00:27:07.930 --> 00:27:10.420
worker find something

00:27:34.990 --> 00:27:35.410
Pastor.

00:28:20.860 --> 00:28:25.160
