If you do not do it, I will.

00:52:27.080 --> 00:52:28.260
Lock disruptors on target.

00:52:28.630 --> 00:52:29.590
Prepare to fire.

00:52:30.440 --> 00:52:31.610
Kaag, you fool!

00:52:43.130 --> 00:52:44.210
Master, hold your fire.

00:52:45.010 --> 00:52:46.550
We could destroy each other here and now.

00:52:46.670 --> 00:52:47.430
Is that what you want?

00:52:48.690 --> 00:52:50.050
It is a good way to die.

00:52:54.500 --> 00:52:57.200
Copernicus found a way to neutralize the bloodworm infection.

00:52:57.280 --> 00:52:59.760
We're beaming survivors aboard this ship even as we speak.

00:53:00.830 --> 00:53:02.790
Then you are dooming your own ship as well.

00:53:03.560 --> 00:53:06.180
I shall be happy to destroy the Enterprise next.

00:53:07.510 --> 00:53:08.790
Show him. Open a channel.

00:53:10.240 --> 00:53:11.520
Look for yourself, Captain.

00:53:20.170 --> 00:53:22.660
Go to Sigme. Energize on my mark.

00:53:26.920 --> 00:53:28.100
I admire his courage.

00:53:29.190 --> 00:53:29.970
It is almost...

00:53:30.220 --> 00:53:33.760
What if this plan succeeds?

00:53:36.420 --> 00:53:40.240
If it succeeds, we will have to destroy them.

00:53:41.740 --> 00:53:43.700
We cannot let the Earthers have this advantage.

00:53:45.340 --> 00:53:46.840
Why not just destroy them now?

00:53:50.060 --> 00:53:52.520
Because there is more to this than meets the eye.

00:54:05.080 --> 00:54:07.340
There's an old saying when you have a Klingon by the tail.

00:54:09.190 --> 00:54:10.110
Klingons have tails?

00:54:22.720 --> 00:54:23.880
Don't do it, Spock.

00:54:24.460 --> 00:54:27.420
Any application of energy into bloodworms could shatter into wavicles.

00:54:28.250 --> 00:54:29.450
To infect the next victim.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:35.520
insidious doctor. According to Dr. Yar's research, the bloodworm form is an aberration.

00:54:36.130 --> 00:54:41.430
It occurs as an interruption of the plasma site's ability to catalyze. If we could repair

00:54:41.430 --> 00:54:46.750
that interruption, it would neutralize the danger posed by the plasma sites. Or they might

00:54:46.750 --> 00:54:58.460
become something even more dangerous. Coy to Kirk. Kirk here. Jim, we've got a problem.

00:55:00.250 --> 00:55:01.670
We're not going to have enough artificial blood.

00:55:02.870 --> 00:55:04.790
We exhausted our stores treating our own wounded.

00:55:05.360 --> 00:55:07.880
I never expected I'd have to replace the blood of 21 people.

00:55:09.150 --> 00:55:10.450
We've got enough for 12.

00:55:11.560 --> 00:55:13.770
If we stretch, 15.

00:55:14.730 --> 00:55:16.840
Bones, I'm not leaving six people behind.

00:55:17.340 --> 00:55:20.280
Jim, you're going to have to ask for blood donors.

00:55:21.550 --> 00:55:21.910
I see.

00:55:23.920 --> 00:55:25.640
All decks, this is the captain speaking.

00:55:26.620 --> 00:55:28.420
We're going to need blood donors to help the Copernicus.

00:55:28.900 --> 00:55:29.980
I'll need 72 bones.

00:55:30.490 --> 00:55:34.570
Make that 71. Report to sickbay.

00:55:37.980 --> 00:55:40.340
70. Permission to leave the bridge, sir?

00:55:41.500 --> 00:55:41.940
69.

00:55:43.630 --> 00:55:44.070
68.

00:55:44.810 --> 00:55:45.250
67.

00:55:45.680 --> 00:55:46.120
66.

00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:50.720
Permission granted, but somebody take the count.

00:55:51.610 --> 00:55:51.890
Miller?

00:55:52.370 --> 00:55:52.670
Aye, sir.

00:56:11.900 --> 00:56:12.760
Steady as she goes.

00:56:20.840 --> 00:56:21.680
They are desperate.

00:56:23.160 --> 00:56:24.320
They will all die.

00:56:25.620 --> 00:56:26.940
Then I shall enjoy watching.

00:56:43.850 --> 00:56:44.150
Captain.

00:56:45.730 --> 00:56:47.550
The Parnicus log is triple encoded, sir.

00:56:47.820 --> 00:56:49.700
I don't know how much of it I'll be able to reconstruct.

00:56:50.570 --> 00:56:52.570
Perhaps Mr. Spock would be more successful.

00:56:57.020 --> 00:56:57.780
I want some answers.

00:56:58.960 --> 00:56:59.960
Who authorized your mission?

00:57:00.730 --> 00:57:05.000
Captain Kirk, this is beyond your authority. It's strictly need to know.

00:57:05.320 --> 00:57:07.800
This is my ship, and I need to know.

00:57:08.650 --> 00:57:10.130
It's a Section 31 operation.

00:57:12.450 --> 00:57:14.540
Section 31. Covert operations.

00:57:15.100 --> 00:57:19.280
Counter operations. Preparedness. The Klingon threats.

00:57:19.900 --> 00:57:22.400
This is the Enterprise, and I'll deal with the Klingons.

00:57:22.560 --> 00:57:27.740
Captain Kirk, can you imagine what would happen if the Klingons spread bloodworms throughout Federation space?

00:57:28.300 --> 00:57:29.980
Yes. The destruction of red blood...

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:34.770
life forms on a catastrophic scale our mission was to find a way of controlling and containing

00:57:34.770 --> 00:57:40.220
plasma sites specifically in the case of open hostilities i have found no evidence of that

00:57:40.220 --> 00:57:49.120
in the copernicus log sir captain something disturbs you you disturb me commander when

00:57:49.440 --> 00:57:53.780
it looked as if we might not survive i ordered the ship's log wiped in the main computer destroyed

00:57:53.990 --> 00:57:59.360
everything we didn't want to take the chance of our research falling into enemy hands captain this

00:57:59.360 --> 00:57:59.920
is the last

00:58:01.220 --> 00:58:07.380
Captain, that's a Priority Blue medical research log. You don't know what it's worth, what this operation cost.

00:58:07.600 --> 00:58:11.230
Oh, I know what it cost. It cost the life of Lieutenant McHale Hodel.

00:58:14.900 --> 00:58:19.670
Copies of this for Spock and McCoy, both science and medical, and anybody else on the ship who needs to know.

00:58:20.630 --> 00:58:24.560
Security, take these two to their quarters and see to it that they stay here.

00:58:59.240 --> 00:58:59.680
Okay, we're next.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.830
No. You and Ensign Kirk will go next.

00:59:03.440 --> 00:59:08.190
Dr. McCoy, you will be needed on the Enterprise to manage the recovery of this team.

00:59:08.630 --> 00:59:12.800
Now, wait a minute, Spock. If anything happens to that young man, the captain will ha-

00:59:12.800 --> 00:59:15.740
Doctor, my Vulcan physiology requires special attention.

00:59:16.210 --> 00:59:20.010
As much as it pains me to say this, you are the best qualified to treat me.

00:59:26.870 --> 00:59:27.310
Jive.

00:59:34.540 --> 00:59:35.960
He sure knows how to swear, doesn't he?

00:59:37.100 --> 00:59:39.340
I thought we were going to need a Vulcan death grip or something.

00:59:39.670 --> 00:59:43.380
There's no such thing as a Vulcan death grip, is there?

00:59:44.790 --> 00:59:46.350
We are not allowed to tell.

01:00:01.630 --> 01:00:03.550
Don't you dare give me any Vulcan blood.

01:00:04.210 --> 01:00:04.950
Shut up.

01:00:09.980 --> 01:00:11.080
We have 13 minutes left.

01:00:11.640 --> 01:00:12.760
You and Peter have to...

01:00:12.760 --> 01:00:13.540
You and Ensign Kirk.

01:00:13.660 --> 01:00:15.070
No, I'm the security guy.

01:00:15.070 --> 01:00:15.910
I go last.

01:00:16.190 --> 01:00:16.330
No.

01:00:16.590 --> 01:00:17.010
Stop it.

01:00:17.310 --> 01:00:18.650
Stop trying to protect me, Spock.

01:00:18.730 --> 01:00:19.550
You're not my uncle.

01:00:19.830 --> 01:00:22.620
Ensign, your courage is admirable, but I am a Vulcan.

01:00:22.760 --> 01:00:24.040
I have greater physical strength.

01:00:24.140 --> 01:00:26.620
Mr. Spock, your Vulcan blood will take twice as long to process.

01:00:26.760 --> 01:00:27.560
You have to go now.

01:00:27.900 --> 01:00:28.960
Alex, you can't stop...

01:00:29.430 --> 01:00:29.970
Argument over.

01:00:30.640 --> 01:00:34.360
You must have learned your bedside manner from Dr. McCoy.

01:00:34.640 --> 01:00:35.660
Take that as a compliment.

01:00:36.250 --> 01:00:37.310
That was not fair, Alex.

01:00:38.760 --> 01:00:39.600
You can yell at me later.

01:00:40.100 --> 01:00:41.500
Now lie down before you fall down.

01:00:44.520 --> 01:00:45.060
You too, sir.

01:00:48.030 --> 01:00:49.640
Here, take this.

01:00:54.600 --> 01:00:55.540
Don't let them get you.

01:00:57.620 --> 01:00:58.100
I won't.

01:01:10.490 --> 01:01:12.110
In a few more minutes, we'll both be home.

01:01:18.960 --> 01:01:19.560
I love you.

01:01:25.230 --> 01:01:25.710
You too.

01:02:02.880 --> 01:02:06.500
Enterprise on my mark stunden bike

01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:36.710
Thank you

01:03:11.230 --> 01:03:12.470
I've injected the hypo.

01:03:12.610 --> 01:03:18.740
You're gonna have to monitor me by remote.

01:03:19.940 --> 01:03:21.000
I won't be able to...

01:03:22.120 --> 01:03:22.380
Oh God!

01:03:34.150 --> 01:03:39.060
Enterprise, the repulsor field is failing. Stay with me.

01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:58.810
Enterprise, the field is to hold them back.

01:04:01.400 --> 01:04:02.780
They are going to lose him.

01:04:04.130 --> 01:04:05.130
That is their weakness.

01:04:06.490 --> 01:04:07.950
They are always overreaching.

01:04:24.940 --> 01:04:25.500
Stay with me.

01:04:26.590 --> 01:04:27.290
We're watching you, Lieutenant.

01:04:27.900 --> 01:04:29.970
As soon as telemetry shows you're clear, we'll be...

01:04:30.060 --> 01:04:37.790
Where's Alex?

01:04:41.130 --> 01:04:41.430
Alex!

01:05:00.480 --> 01:05:18.970
where is alex peter are you there alex alex are you okay yeah stay with me peter alex i'm here

01:05:18.970 --> 01:05:22.900
it's another minute enterprise i'm almost there

01:05:33.390 --> 01:05:43.520
Oh God, Enterprise, Pulsar Field has failed.

01:05:43.840 --> 01:05:45.020
Somebody do something!

01:05:45.240 --> 01:05:48.860
Scotty, who's safe place to put him down, Captain?

01:05:54.510 --> 01:05:59.960
Eric, I'm so...

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:00.900
I'm so sorry, I...

01:06:01.560 --> 01:06:02.260
Alex!

01:06:04.340 --> 01:06:05.400
I thought I had more time.

01:06:06.320 --> 01:06:07.440
Somebody help him!

01:06:12.690 --> 01:06:13.930
Guess I'm gonna need this after all.

01:06:14.730 --> 01:06:16.130
Hang on Freeman, you're almost there.

01:06:17.610 --> 01:06:17.970
Alex!

01:06:22.120 --> 01:06:23.140
Freeman, don't do it.

01:06:23.270 --> 01:06:24.010
This isn't the answer.

01:06:24.910 --> 01:06:25.740
Alex feeds!

01:06:28.400 --> 01:06:28.560
Peter!

01:06:30.480 --> 01:06:31.700
Alex, don't go!

01:06:37.110 --> 01:06:38.150
Peter, I love you.

01:06:39.360 --> 01:06:40.120
I love you too.

01:06:43.580 --> 01:06:52.650
Freeman, hang on for just a moment longer.

01:06:53.440 --> 01:06:53.620
Freeman!

01:07:00.820 --> 01:07:18.900
Shut that thing off. Shut that goddamn thing off.

01:07:32.750 --> 01:07:33.530
Bones, how are you feeling?

01:07:34.390 --> 01:07:35.690
Like Scotty after shore leave.

01:07:36.380 --> 01:07:37.160
I'm fine, too.

01:07:40.040 --> 01:07:41.160
He's hurting pretty badly, Jim.

01:07:54.450 --> 01:07:57.540
It's my fault he's dead.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:04.780
If I hadn't have gone, there would have been one less person to rescue.

01:08:07.830 --> 01:08:08.850
He'd still be alive.

01:08:14.300 --> 01:08:14.820
You were right.

01:08:17.380 --> 01:08:18.260
I shouldn't have gone.

01:08:19.960 --> 01:08:23.400
Peter, you did your job, and you were right.

01:08:23.540 --> 01:08:25.680
I was trying to protect you.

01:08:27.600 --> 01:08:28.940
You're the only family I have left.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:40.500
Alex was my family. You were never there. You were always out in space somewhere. I have

01:08:40.500 --> 01:08:41.140
no family.

01:08:49.450 --> 01:08:50.170
Should've found a way.

01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:51.840
You did your job.

01:08:53.220 --> 01:08:59.000
Ah, Spock is right. The Enterprise, crew, you.

01:09:01.340 --> 01:09:05.280
You're my family. You're all that I've ever had.

01:09:05.340 --> 01:09:10.230
If it had been you.

01:09:10.410 --> 01:09:13.950
If it had been me, Jim, you would not have done anything different.

01:09:18.740 --> 01:09:19.060
Captain.

01:09:38.070 --> 01:09:42.160
Garg, you've seen the evidence. Do you believe me now?

01:09:44.640 --> 01:09:50.860
I've not solved anything, Kirk. You have made it worse. Your Federation will use the bloodworms as a weapon.

01:09:52.060 --> 01:09:59.880
I have to destroy you. I will make you a trade cap. You will give me a copy of your data file.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:05.990
And I would not destroy your ship or I give you my files and you destroy my ship anyway

01:10:06.810 --> 01:10:10.910
Garg I trust you about as much as you trust me so

01:10:11.350 --> 01:10:29.540
Pears I have an earth to bite the tail. I cannot hang on and I cannot let go. We cannot destroy the Copernicus

01:10:30.220 --> 01:10:35.960
If we use phasers, or photon torpedoes, to destroy her, it will generate a very large cloud of wavicles.

01:10:37.240 --> 01:10:40.770
Conceivably, they could find their way to another ship, or even a planet.

01:10:41.490 --> 01:10:44.010
Wouldn't they burn up once they entered the tail from the red star?

01:10:44.660 --> 01:10:50.210
The red giant isn't hot enough. The wavicles will use the energy of the star to reproduce at an incredible rate.

01:10:50.690 --> 01:10:54.740
The star will become a gigantic incubator, forever.

01:10:55.480 --> 01:10:59.430
So, this is what your starfic research has created, Kirk.

01:11:00.250 --> 01:11:09.560
death for everyone and you call klingons warmongers you do have a solution don't you spock bones the

01:11:10.090 --> 01:11:16.960
plasma sites are not a disease they are a diseased life form the healthy form of the wavicle is benign

01:11:16.960 --> 01:11:22.380
it uses oxygen only as a catalyst for transformation the particle form is an

01:11:22.380 --> 01:11:22.840
interruption.

01:11:23.400 --> 01:11:25.680
Jim, there is a cure.

01:11:27.120 --> 01:11:29.800
YARM was reversed by engineering of plasma sites.

01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:37.080
A binding mechanism would reboot the catalyst back to its ancestral state and allow them to complete their natural life cycle.

01:11:37.750 --> 01:11:40.430
But Dr. Yar did not have time to complete the synthesis.

01:11:40.960 --> 01:11:46.310
We can manufacture the catalytics. Fontana's already working on it. It's not a difficult process.

01:11:46.660 --> 01:11:53.610
But the plasmacytes will only be able to access the catalytic elements in a human bloodstream. It would require a volunteer.

01:11:54.460 --> 01:11:55.940
It would be a suicide mission, Jim.

01:11:56.620 --> 01:11:58.260
No, I'm not going to authorize it.

01:11:59.380 --> 01:11:59.660
Jim.

01:12:00.190 --> 01:12:02.070
I'm running out of boxes to think outside of.

01:12:03.420 --> 01:12:06.280
Less than two hours ago, you were prepared to destroy the Copernicus.

01:12:06.550 --> 01:12:08.210
This is one instead of 21.

01:12:08.710 --> 01:12:10.110
It's still one too many, Spock.

01:12:10.190 --> 01:12:11.930
Nevertheless, logic compels that we...

01:12:11.930 --> 01:12:13.350
To hell with your logic, Spock.

01:12:13.880 --> 01:12:14.720
Are you volunteering?

01:12:15.290 --> 01:12:16.630
My blood is unsuitable, Doctor.

01:12:17.120 --> 01:12:17.800
Yours, however...

01:12:17.800 --> 01:12:18.480
Gentlemen, stop.

01:12:25.970 --> 01:12:26.970
We have a volunteer.

01:12:30.190 --> 01:12:31.990
No, absolutely not.

01:12:32.230 --> 01:12:34.690
Stop being my uncle and be my captain.

01:12:35.310 --> 01:12:35.910
Not this way.

01:12:36.400 --> 01:12:39.120
If I don't go, someone else will have to go instead.

01:12:40.290 --> 01:12:41.610
I should be the one to do this.

01:12:43.990 --> 01:12:45.090
Let me be with Alex.

01:12:45.430 --> 01:12:47.550
Peter, you're speaking from grief.

01:12:48.040 --> 01:12:48.780
This isn't rational.

01:12:49.270 --> 01:12:51.090
Captain, I've examined him.

01:12:51.290 --> 01:12:53.640
He's physically and mentally fit.

01:12:54.820 --> 01:12:57.100
Jim, we are running out of time.

01:12:58.880 --> 01:12:59.440
Give it to me.

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:03.780
Don't do it, Montana. Try it, and I'll declare you unfit for duty.

01:13:04.440 --> 01:13:06.330
You psych-demonious bastard.

01:13:06.900 --> 01:13:09.330
Accident of birth. You're still not going.

01:13:09.530 --> 01:13:12.390
Jim, there is one other thing you should know.

01:13:13.180 --> 01:13:16.040
This is the part of the law Lieutenant Uhura could not decrypt.

01:13:21.780 --> 01:13:24.820
Fair enough of your trust to ask you to hold your fire just a little while longer.

01:13:26.470 --> 01:13:29.050
I'll take this much fun since I assassinated my grandfather.

01:13:30.600 --> 01:13:32.200
What is it you want to show me now?

01:13:33.370 --> 01:13:37.660
The truth. Security to the bridge on the double.

01:13:51.190 --> 01:13:52.970
I'm going to introduce you to a human concept.

01:13:54.370 --> 01:13:55.150
We call it trust.

01:13:55.450 --> 01:13:57.150
Kyle, shut down the weapon systems.

01:13:58.500 --> 01:13:58.900
That's an order.

01:14:00.700 --> 01:14:03.970
A condition necessary for betrayal.

01:14:04.190 --> 01:14:06.960
This is Mackle Blodgett and Jenna Yar.

01:14:07.220 --> 01:14:09.820
The two officers responsible for this entire situation.

01:14:10.410 --> 01:14:12.100
Captain, what are you doing?

01:14:12.910 --> 01:14:15.930
You want to give me one good reason why I shouldn't share your information with the Klingons?

01:14:16.070 --> 01:14:22.740
It would neutralize our advantage. It would give them a weapon.

01:14:24.150 --> 01:14:26.290
This isn't a weapon the Klingons want, it's dishonorable.

01:14:27.160 --> 01:14:29.450
Honor, come on Klingons!

01:14:30.480 --> 01:14:32.320
More honor, apparently, than among some humans.

01:14:33.740 --> 01:14:37.360
Your mission had absolutely nothing to do with ending the plasma site infestation.

01:14:39.820 --> 01:14:42.440
The Copernicus was headed for Klingon space.

01:14:44.100 --> 01:14:44.860
Fight your fire!

01:14:45.250 --> 01:14:46.190
Carp, hold your fire!

01:14:46.850 --> 01:14:47.750
You need to hear all this.

01:14:49.470 --> 01:14:51.800
Captain, the Klingons started this war.

01:14:51.960 --> 01:14:54.830
It was a big mistake.

01:14:56.110 --> 01:14:57.270
They underestimated us.

01:14:59.050 --> 01:14:59.970
We'll be sequ...

01:15:02.280 --> 01:15:02.720
Consequences?

01:15:02.920 --> 01:15:07.050
If we don't do this, they will.

01:15:07.400 --> 01:15:07.820
Do what?

01:15:08.510 --> 01:15:08.970
Say it.

01:15:09.430 --> 01:15:12.790
Use the bloodworms to end the Klingon threat once and for all.

01:15:13.090 --> 01:15:13.530
Genocide?

01:15:14.120 --> 01:15:14.800
You're insane.

01:15:15.290 --> 01:15:16.950
I'm the sanest one here, Doctor.

01:15:17.560 --> 01:15:20.740
If you're not with us, you're with the Klingons.

01:15:21.400 --> 01:15:22.480
Are you getting all this, Karg?

01:15:23.110 --> 01:15:26.880
Looks as if you want me to destroy you.

01:15:28.420 --> 01:15:29.840
This is what blind hatred looks like.

01:15:30.600 --> 01:15:31.640
Is it going to solve anything?

01:15:32.450 --> 01:15:34.050
Is it going to end our bloodworm problem?

01:15:36.000 --> 01:15:40.040
When the Copernicus hits the flare, the bloodworms are going to be released on a galactic scale.

01:15:41.500 --> 01:15:43.590
We have the own events.

01:15:45.950 --> 01:15:47.150
And the crew of the Copernicus.

01:15:48.140 --> 01:15:49.180
And all those that have died.

01:15:49.900 --> 01:15:50.900
Is this what they died for?

01:15:56.590 --> 01:15:59.970
Dark, are you courageous enough to trust in Earth?

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:04.670
Earthman, again, I propose peace.

01:16:06.120 --> 01:16:07.620
Hangons do not make peace.

01:16:08.580 --> 01:16:09.860
And how is that working for you, Karg?

01:16:11.470 --> 01:16:12.750
How many ships have you lost?

01:16:14.510 --> 01:16:17.600
How many friends, colleagues, family members?

01:16:18.750 --> 01:16:20.550
How's that working for the Empire these days?

01:16:24.390 --> 01:16:26.110
Karg, this is a far greater challenge.

01:16:28.130 --> 01:16:29.970
We must work together to solve this problem.

01:16:31.980 --> 01:16:33.880
Are you as great as your legend says you are?

01:16:35.400 --> 01:16:38.180
You appeal to my vanity, Kirk. I like that.

01:16:39.170 --> 01:16:42.020
You are audacious, Captain. I like that, too.

01:16:43.620 --> 01:16:47.080
But that is still no reason to trust you or any other Earther.

01:16:48.940 --> 01:16:56.080
A reason. A reason. I'll give you a reason.

01:17:01.500 --> 01:17:04.640
Here it is, Dr. Yar. Here it is.

01:17:06.020 --> 01:17:06.460
The cure.

01:17:07.940 --> 01:17:08.460
Save it.

01:17:09.490 --> 01:17:13.820
Because all it's going to take is one person sacrificing themselves to save us all.

01:17:16.220 --> 01:17:16.900
One volunteer.

01:17:17.140 --> 01:17:22.770
It's going to be Karg, my nephew Peter.

01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:26.640
Because I sure as hell don't see one damn Klingon volunteering.

01:17:28.000 --> 01:17:28.680
Is that your challenge?

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:32.320
You are just looking for another way to save your nephew.

01:17:33.170 --> 01:17:34.130
You can't do this, Kirk.

01:17:34.520 --> 01:17:35.500
I won't let you.

01:17:37.680 --> 01:17:38.860
A repulsor jar, Captain.

01:17:39.710 --> 01:17:40.090
Yes.

01:17:41.130 --> 01:17:41.530
Plasmasites.

01:17:47.210 --> 01:17:49.150
Everybody, do you see what I have here?

01:17:55.550 --> 01:17:56.530
Tell them to back off, Kirk.

01:17:58.760 --> 01:17:59.460
Everybody stand down.

01:17:59.580 --> 01:17:59.960
That's an order.

01:18:04.280 --> 01:18:05.260
What do you want, Blodgett?

01:18:06.370 --> 01:18:09.150
Starfleet doesn't have the courage to use these on the Klingons.

01:18:09.620 --> 01:18:10.220
I do.

01:18:10.900 --> 01:18:12.640
My thumb comes off this button,

01:18:13.010 --> 01:18:15.670
you'll all have bloodworms crawling up your guts.

01:18:16.060 --> 01:18:18.860
Well, thank you for finally telling the truth about the Copernicus real mission.

01:18:19.420 --> 01:18:22.730
Garg, how would you have reacted if you'd known this from the beginning?

01:18:23.660 --> 01:18:24.960
Do you even have to ask?

01:18:25.940 --> 01:18:28.100
We will bring your bloodworms back to you.

01:18:29.380 --> 01:18:29.980
It will be a...

01:18:31.410 --> 01:18:37.690
You son of a bitch! You killed all those people! You killed Alex!

01:18:37.910 --> 01:18:39.530
Put that phaser down! That's an order!

01:18:40.190 --> 01:18:43.280
He shoots me. It'll be the Copernicus all over again!

01:18:45.700 --> 01:18:48.850
I'm fully prepared to destroy the ship if that's what it takes to stop you.

01:18:50.450 --> 01:18:53.000
Peter, Starfleet handled this.

01:18:53.400 --> 01:18:56.760
Starfleet? His mission was authorized by Starfleet!

01:18:56.950 --> 01:18:58.490
Not the Starfleet we serve, Peter.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:01.120
aside, sir.

01:19:01.320 --> 01:19:05.080
Ensign Kirk, I will not allow you to lower yourself

01:19:05.080 --> 01:19:06.000
to this man's level.

01:19:09.480 --> 01:19:14.300
Peter, hatred is the right.

01:19:16.310 --> 01:19:18.250
We don't want the Enterprise infected with it anymore

01:19:18.250 --> 01:19:20.390
than we want it infected with blood borers.

01:19:21.040 --> 01:19:22.580
This isn't about the Enterprise.

01:19:24.080 --> 01:19:25.080
This is for Alex.

01:19:25.450 --> 01:19:25.890
You're right.

01:19:30.410 --> 01:19:37.230
better than anyone. Is this what he'd want for you? To murder? To kill in his name?

01:19:38.670 --> 01:19:57.340
He wanted. He only wanted. You loved him. I know how much I loved him.

01:20:01.020 --> 01:20:04.420
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

01:20:04.740 --> 01:20:07.870
Should've sued.

01:20:21.960 --> 01:20:22.540
Damn you!

01:20:24.220 --> 01:20:24.540
F*** you!

01:20:26.900 --> 01:20:27.860
What are you doing?!

01:20:38.890 --> 01:20:42.740
Security, get this bastard off my bridge.

01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:52.940
Ugh, you.

01:21:06.880 --> 01:21:11.930
Captain Kirk, I believe I've solved the problem of your plasmasites.

01:21:13.080 --> 01:21:14.480
Beam me over to the Copernicus.

01:21:15.890 --> 01:21:20.660
I went along with this because I wanted to solve the mystery of the plasmasites.

01:21:28.530 --> 01:21:29.550
It has to end here.

01:21:30.020 --> 01:21:33.440
Now. All of it. I'm going to stop all of this.

01:21:33.700 --> 01:21:35.700
Damn it, Yar. We can save you.

01:21:36.170 --> 01:21:37.750
So someone else can die? No.

01:21:39.560 --> 01:21:45.120
Ensign Kirk, I'm so sorry about your loss, but this is my responsibility, not yours.

01:21:48.780 --> 01:21:50.020
Plasma sites are sick.

01:22:17.180 --> 01:22:29.900
daughter. You get back to Earth. Will you tell her everything? Don't leave anything out.

01:22:30.890 --> 01:22:39.460
Just ask one day that she remember me, Jenna Natasha Yar.

01:23:00.570 --> 01:23:03.470
Scotty wanted to beam over to think about this.

01:23:25.320 --> 01:23:26.950
Price, are you monitoring?

01:23:27.540 --> 01:23:28.040
Or watching?

01:23:50.670 --> 01:23:50.870
I'm tired.

01:24:05.948 --> 01:24:06.948
It doesn't hurt.

01:24:07.420 --> 01:24:08.460
It doesn't hurt at all.

01:25:11.870 --> 01:25:14.650
This is a sparkle dancer.

01:25:17.500 --> 01:25:18.340
I'll be dear.

01:25:19.050 --> 01:25:19.170
Beautiful.

01:25:49.900 --> 01:25:50.400
Police.

01:25:51.340 --> 01:25:52.360
That's a push for home.

01:25:52.620 --> 01:25:53.620
That's stupid!

01:26:04.188 --> 01:26:04.688
Fascinating.

01:26:44.940 --> 01:26:46.940
Are you gonna have me court-martialed?

01:26:47.372 --> 01:26:47.872
No.

01:26:49.580 --> 01:26:50.700
Because I'm your nephew?

01:26:52.172 --> 01:26:53.172
Peace.

01:26:53.324 --> 01:26:54.164
I don't need to be fair.

01:26:55.756 --> 01:26:56.756
I need to be smart.

01:26:58.156 --> 01:26:59.536
When you make a mistake it's...

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:01.000
There's not a reason to quit.

01:27:02.364 --> 01:27:03.204
It's a lesson to learn.

01:27:06.268 --> 01:27:06.948
Are you learning, Peter?

01:27:09.532 --> 01:27:11.532
Are you going to have me transfer to the Enterprise?

01:27:15.164 --> 01:27:15.764
What do you want?

01:27:20.284 --> 01:27:20.884
I want to stay.

01:27:22.748 --> 01:27:23.248
Here.

01:27:25.116 --> 01:27:25.956
Where Alex served.

01:27:30.604 --> 01:27:31.604
Good.

01:27:33.324 --> 01:27:34.284
Because I want you to stay.

01:27:43.212 --> 01:27:44.592
In ancient times when I...

01:27:45.196 --> 01:27:46.536
A warrior fell in battle.

01:27:48.236 --> 01:27:50.796
They'd put him on a boat with his sword and his shield.

01:27:51.916 --> 01:27:52.996
Send him off in flames.

01:27:55.628 --> 01:27:56.788
Godspeed, McHale Hotel.

01:27:58.476 --> 01:27:58.976
Godspeed.

01:28:01.880 --> 01:28:04.370
Godspeed, Alex Freeman Kirk.

01:28:06.480 --> 01:28:11.040
That's sailing.

01:28:14.380 --> 01:28:14.820
Godspeed.

01:28:20.170 --> 01:28:24.060
I loved it so much.

01:28:26.610 --> 01:28:27.630
And it hurts, Uncle Jim.

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:55.610
so much. I know, Peter. I know. Look.

01:30:10.650 --> 01:30:13.810
Gentlemen, space is not the final frontier.

01:30:16.220 --> 01:30:16.920
The final frontier.

01:30:18.860 --> 01:30:21.870
So, space is where we'll meet the challenge.

01:30:26.780 --> 01:30:27.220
Chekov.

01:30:27.630 --> 01:30:29.160
And of course, Kyle.

01:30:30.440 --> 01:30:30.880
Take a sound.
